      "text": "To find the difference between the total number of green tiles and blue tiles in the new figure, we need to determine the new number of green and blue tiles first, and then calculate the difference.\n\nThe original figure is a rhombus made up of 13 blue tiles and 6 green tiles. When a border of green tiles is added around the figure, we can count the number of new green tiles added.\n\nThe new figure consists of 28 left-facing rhombuses and 10 right-facing rhombuses (since there are 28 blue tiles and 10 white tiles). Each left-facing rhombus has 14 new green tiles (4 from the two blue tiles in the center of the rhombus, and 12 from the sides), and each right-facing rhombus has 8 new green tiles (4 from the two blue tiles in the center of the rhombus, and 4 from the sides).\n\nTherefore, the new figure has:\n\n38 green tiles because there are 28 + 10 = 38 green tiles.\n\nThe difference between the total number of green tiles and blue tiles in the new figure is then:\n\n38 – 13 = 25.\n\nThus, the answer is $\\boxed{25}$.",
